# Frame-rate independence (tests/fps_check.py): the same inputs at different
# frame rates (DOTHEROES_FPS, DIAG_VBLANK_MS), the game's state compared.
# Needs DOTHEROES_DEV_STATE=1, DOTHEROES_DEV_KEYS=1 (the marks), DOTHEROES_DEV_MEMSNAP=1
# (the two snapshots for the game's clocks), DOTHEROES_DEV_PLAYER_LOG=1 (the hero's
# object every 4 ms), PS3_FTRACE + DOTHEROES_PHYS_STATS=1 (frames, physics), and a
# save at the castle with the sword (SAVES=).
#   mark 1 -> 2   standing still for 10 s, guest memory at both ends: the game's
#                 clocks (tests/native/find_state.cpp clocks)
#   mark 2 -> 3   walking down 1 s: distance (the camera target, no clamp there)
#   mark 3 -> 4   walking back up 1 s
#   mark 4 -> 5   to the grass by the first cliff and cutting it: the debris'
#                 physics -- steps a second, bodies, how long it lasts. The
#                 hero's speed differs a little with the frame rate (the game
#                 truncates each frame's step to 0.01), so the route ends its
#                 moves against walls (0.65 s right, so walking down stops at
#                 the ledge; 1.5 s left, to the wall) rather than by time; the
#                 sword presses are 0.5 s apart, longer than a swing at 30 fps
#                 (~466 ms; ~400 above), so every press swings at every rate
#   mark 5 -> 6   standing still 30 s while the debris settles
log TitleMovie 120
sleep 5
press START
sleep 3
press START
sleep 5
press CROSS
state life>0,area==17 60
sleep 5
touch mark.trigger
touch memsnap.trigger
sleep 10
touch memsnap.trigger
touch mark.trigger
sleep 3
hold DOWN 1
sleep 2
touch mark.trigger
hold UP 1
sleep 2
touch mark.trigger
hold RIGHT 0.65
hold DOWN 5
hold LEFT 1.5
hold RIGHT 0.15
repeat 6 CROSS 0.5
sleep 4
hold RIGHT 0.6
repeat 6 CROSS 0.5
touch mark.trigger
sleep 30
touch mark.trigger
sleep 2
